10 REM DATA, READ AND RESTORE: A PRICE LIST
20 READ N
30 FOR I = 1 TO N
40   READ ITEM$, PRICE
50   PRINT ITEM$; TAB(16); PRICE
60 NEXT I
70 REM RESTORE N MOVES THE DATA POINTER TO A LINE
80 RESTORE 1020
90 READ ITEM$, PRICE
100 PRINT "AGAIN: "; ITEM$; " COSTS "; PRICE
110 REM RESTORE ALONE GOES BACK TO THE FIRST ITEM
120 RESTORE
130 READ N, FIRST$
140 PRINT "THE LIST HAS "; N; " ITEMS, STARTING WITH "; FIRST$
150 END
1000 DATA 3
1010 DATA APPLE, 0.5
1020 DATA "BREAD, SLICED", 2.25
1030 DATA HOT DOG, 1.2
